{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "יזיד", :translit "yazid", :gloss "presumptuously schemes"} {:he "אך הנביא אשר יזיד לדבר דבר בשמי", :translit "akh ha-navi asher yazid le-daber davar bi-shmi", :gloss "but the prophet who presumptuously speaks a word in My name"} {:he "שהחזיר הנביא אשר בא בדבר השם", :translit "she-hechezir ha-navi asher ba bi-dvar ha-shem", :gloss "who caused the prophet who came with the word of HaShem to turn back"} {:he "וכחש לו", :translit "ve-kichesh lo", :gloss "and lied to him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["יזיד" "אך הנביא אשר יזיד לדבר דבר בשמי"]}], :frame {:text "The prophet from Judah who came to Bethel was killed by a lion because he turned back to eat bread at the false prophet's urging, violating HaShem's direct command (1 Kings 13:20-24). The verse in Deuteronomy 18:20 prescribes death for the prophet who presumptuously speaks what HaShem did not command. The story of the prophet at Bethel is told in 1 Kings 13.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 18:20" "1 Kings 13:20-24"]}} {:quotes [{:he "על רעהו", :translit "al re'ehu", :gloss "against his fellow"} {:he "כאשר יקום איש על רעהו", :translit "ka-asher yakum ish al re'ehu", :gloss "when a man rises against his fellow"} {:he "ושעיר על רעהו יקרא", :translit "ve-se'ir al re'ehu yikkare", :gloss "and Seir against his fellow is called"} {:he "כי מפלת אדום כה תאמרו איש על רעהו", :translit "ki mi-plat edom koh tomeru ish al re'ehu", :gloss "concerning the downfall of Edom, thus shall you say, each man to his fellow"} {:he "גבר מחליק על רעהו", :translit "gever machlik al re'ehu", :gloss "a man flatters his fellow"} {:he "ורצחו נפש", :translit "ve-ratzacho nefesh", :gloss "and murdered a soul"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["על רעהו" "כאשר יקום איש על רעהו" "ושעיר על רעהו יקרא" "כי מפלת אדום כה תאמרו איש על רעהו" "גבר מחליק על רעהו"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase in Isaiah occurs at Isaiah 21:11. The phrase regarding false prophets appears at Micah 7:5, where the context warns against trusting a neighbor or friend in a time of moral collapse. The term for flattery with smooth lips recalls Psalm 12:3, which describes those who speak with a double heart and flattering lips.", :sources ["Isaiah 21:11" "Micah 7:5" "Psalm 12:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בערמה", :translit "be-ormah", :gloss "with cunning"} {:he "ויעשו גם המה בערמה", :translit "va-ya'asu gam hemah be-ormah", :gloss "they also acted with cunning"} {:he "מעם מזבחי תקחנו למות", :translit "me-im mizbechi tikachenu le-mavet", :gloss "from My altar you shall take him to death"} {:he "חוטבי עצים ושואבי מים למזבח", :translit "chotvei etzim ve-sho'avei mayim la-mizbeach", :gloss "woodcutters and water-drawers for the altar"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["בערמה" "ויעשו גם המה בערמה"]}], :frame {:text "The Gibeonites deceived Joshua into making a covenant, and as a result became woodcutters and water-drawers for the congregation and the altar (Joshua 9:4, 9:23, 9:27). The Exodus verse about taking a murderer from God's altar to die is Exodus 21:14. Rabbenu Asher (the Rosh) drew the contrast: the Gibeonites' cunning drew them near to Israel and the altar, while the presumptuous killer's cunning distances him from both.", :sources ["Joshua 9:4" "Joshua 9:23" "Joshua 9:27" "Exodus 21:14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["יזיד" "אך הנביא אשר יזיד לדבר דבר בשמי"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "יזיד", :refs ["Deuteronomy 18:20"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אך הנביא אשר יזיד לדבר דבר בשמי", :refs ["Deuteronomy 18:20"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["על רעהו" "כאשר יקום איש על רעהו" "ושעיר על רעהו יקרא" "כי מפלת אדום כה תאמרו איש על רעהו" "גבר מחליק על רעהו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "על רעהו", :refs ["Exodus 21:14" "Deuteronomy 22:26" "Isaiah 34:14" "Jeremiah 23:35" "Proverbs 29:5"], :n 5, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כאשר יקום איש על רעהו", :refs ["Deuteronomy 22:26"]